From 63c26995181e681dca90f173a7d2a63ac37be9d3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 11:52:32 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] fix(prim3): publish the lattice-learning runtime the
 reviewed-mission page imports (W5)

js/prim3-mission/released-app.mjs and released-learning.mjs imported
PRIM3/game/halo/adaptive/topology-learning.mjs, and deploy-pages.yml strips
all of PRIM3/ from the published tree: the exported reviewed-mission page
would load without its learning runtime. This is the second private-tree
import of its kind; audit W1 fixed the first (the generated-recipe compiler).

Promote the runtime the same way W1 did: copy it byte-identical to
js/prim3-mission/topology-learning.mjs (git sees a 100% copy), point both
published importers, the Worker and the unit test at it, and leave the
private path as a one-line re-export so the adaptive engine beside it keeps
resolving with no second copy. The Equity Uprise source map follows the file
(the shim no longer names the product); its coverage report is regenerated.

The new test in scripts/test/prim3-topology-learning.test.mjs fails on the
PR head (both importers reach into PRIM3/ and the private file is the only
copy) and passes here. Merged with the deep-audit branch, which carries
scripts/test/published-import-closure.test.mjs, the closure test fails on
the PR head naming both importers and passes with this change.

